{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "ts-psi-readers",
  "gate": "required",
  "operation": "ts-psi-readers",
  "candidate": "transport-views-worker",
  "worker_operation": "ts-psi-",
  "contract": [
    "Read every carrier via TransportFramer and the PAT and PMT PIDs via SectionAssembler, PatReader, PatCollector and PmtReader. Fold the accepted current PAT and latest current PMTs, in table order, using the declared descriptor namespace.",
    "Drain each physical transport entity independently. Reference FFmpeg formats opens MPEG-TS with a preloaded byte source and calls av_read_frame to EOF with codec parsers and timestamp fill disabled.",
    "Fold kind 5 program rows (subkind 0: program number, PMT PID, PCR PID, signed PMT version), followed by member streams in observable order. The absent PMT has PCR PID zero and version -1. A stream the demuxer discovers from PES on a PID that no PMT lists has no PSI program membership and is not folded; the PSI readers never see PES.",
    "Fold kind 5 stream rows (subkind 1: program number, PID, codec tag, hearing-impaired flag, visual-impaired flag), then length-prefixed codec name (subkind 2), language bytes (subkind 3) and DVB subtitle initialization (subkind 4, composition and ancillary page words and type for each service). The standalone projection uses a valid HEVC or EAC3 registration identifier as the published codec tag for the corresponding stream. MPEG audio is represented as one codec family because the stream_type does not identify the exact audio layer. Initialization outside DVB subtitle signalling is outside this comparison.",
    "Fold kind 7 for clean end and kind 8 for source refusal."
  ],
  "required_profiles": [
    "atsc",
    "dvb",
    "ts188",
    "ts192"
  ],
  "required_targets": [
    "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu",
    "thumbv7neon-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"
  ],
  "iterations": 50,
  "minimum_pairs": 30,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "reference": "ffmpeg-transport-views-native",
  "runner": "cargo xtask report",
